  "question": {
    "text": "If a circle passes through the point $(a, b)$ and cuts the circle $x^2+y^2=p^2$ orthogonally, then the equation of the locus of its centre is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FMS7i",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2-3 a x-4 b y+\\left(a^2+b^2-p^2\\right)=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "99Ymc",
      "text": "\n$2 a x+2 b y-\\left(a^2-b^2+p^2\\right)=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WlP7y",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2-2 a x-3 b y+\\left(a^2-b^2-p^2\\right)=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "x1ks4",
      "text": "\n$2 a x+2 b y-\\left(a^2+b^2+p^2\\right)=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the centre be $(\\alpha, \\beta)$\n$\\because$ It cut the circle $\\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{y}^2=\\mathrm{p}^2$ orthogonally\n$2(-\\alpha) \\times 0+2(-\\beta) \\times 0=c_1-p^2$\n$\\mathrm{c}_1=\\mathrm{p}^2$\nLet equation of circle is $x^2+y^2-2 \\alpha x-2 \\beta y+p^2=0$\nIt pass through $(a, b) \\Rightarrow a^2+b^2-2 \\alpha a-2 \\beta b+p^2=0$\nLocus $\\therefore 2 a x+2 b y-\\left(a^2+b^2+p^2\\right)=0$",
    "image": null
  },
